<p class="sub-head"><a name="Zoom_commands"></a>Zoom commands</p>
<p class="whs19">They are used for zooming the scene.</p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="808" class="whs20">
<col class="whs21">
<col class="whs22">
<col class="whs23">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="17.12%" class="whs24">
<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="73.505%" class="whs25">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="9.375%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Zoom All</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Resets the view extents to fit the visible data.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Zoom_All.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Zoom In</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Magnifies the visible data twice.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Zoom_In.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Zoom Out</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Recedes the visible data twice.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Zoom_Out.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs31">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Zoom Selected</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs32">
<p class="normal-table">Resets the view extents to fit the visible selected data.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Zoom_Selected.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; font-weight:bold;">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Commands_for_switching_mouse_operations_mode"></a>Commands for switching mouse operations mode</p>
<p>These commands are used for switching the mode for mouse operations on the viewable area. Th<span lang="EN-US">e</span>s<span lang="EN-US">e</span> mode<span lang="EN-US">s are</span> stored so next time when you <span lang="EN-US">open new window</span> <span class="Mode">Zoom Window</span> <span lang="EN-US">will be enabled by default.</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="807" class="whs33">
<col class="whs21">
<col class="whs22">
<col class="whs23">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="17.12%" class="whs24">
<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="73.505%" class="whs25">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="9.375%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Zoom Window</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Resets the view extents to fit the visible data in the rectangle that is drawn by the mouse.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/zoom_window.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Zoom Mode</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Zooms in or out depending on the mouse move – up or down. Hold down the left mouse button and move the mouse up or down to zoom in or out.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Zoom_Mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Rotate</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Switches to Rotate mode.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Rotate.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Pan</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Switches to Pan mode.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Pan.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Viewport_Rendering_Context_Window"></a>Render mode commands</p>
<p>They are used for visualisation of all objects in the scene.</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../working_with_data/visualisation_files/image016.gif" width="342px" height="194px" border="0" class="img_whs34" alt=""></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="807" class="whs35">
<col class="whs21">
<col class="whs22">
<col class="whs23">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="17.12%" class="whs24">
<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="73.505%" class="whs25">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="9.375%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Points</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Draw scan data<span lang="EN-US">’s</span> and meshes<span lang="EN-US">’ vertices</span> as points in the scene during rotate, pan, and zoom actions. This command is equivalent to the Points option in ‘On Rotate/Pan’ group from Display Settings dialog. This mode is by default and is not stored so next time when you run KUBE Draw Points will be used.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Rendering_Points_and_Points_Mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Large Points</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Draw only objects’ vertices as large points.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Rendering_Large_Points_and_Large_Points_Mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Wireframe</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Draw objects as connected triangles. Triangles are used for scan data and meshes only. Polylines are drawn as connected lines.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Rendering_Polygons_and_Polygons_Mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Flat</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Draw objects as connected triangles each of which is shaded depending on the angle of its normal to the light direction in the scene. This mode is applied for scan data and meshes only.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Rendering_Flat_and_Flat_Shaded_Mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func">Flat + Wireframe</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Draw objects as combination of flat shaded surface and wireframe.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/rendering_flat_wireframe_and_flat_wireframe_mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Smooth</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Draw objects as smooth shaded surface. Shading is the same as in <span class="Mode">Flat</span> mode, but there is an approximation of the hue between neighbouring triangles. This mode is applied for scan data and meshes only.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Rendering_Smooth_and_Smooth_Shaded_Mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func">Smooth + Wireframe</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table"><span style="text-underline:none;">Draw objects as combination of smooth shaded surface and wireframe.</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/rendering_smooth_wireframe_and_smooth_wireframe_mode.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func">Display Boundaries</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table"><span style="text-underline:none;">Draw mesh boundary as connected line.</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/display_boundaries.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func">Toggle Wireframe</p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Switches between shaded (Flat, Smooth) and shaded + Wireframe modes.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Toggle_Wireframe.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Viewport_On_Rotate_Pan_Context_Window"></a>On Rotate/Pan commands</p>
<p>They are used for visualisation of all objects (excluding datum entities) in the scene during rotate, pan, and zoom actions.</p>
<p><img src="../Working_with_data/Visualisation_files/image017.gif" width="323px" height="174px" border="0" class="img_whs36" alt=""></p>
<p>These commands are divided into two sub-groups.</p>
<p class="sub-head-steptitle">Commands related to the details of objects</p>
<p>They are not applicable when <span class="Mode">Draw Scene</span> mode is enabled. Th<span lang="EN-US">e</span>s<span lang="EN-US">e</span> mode<span lang="EN-US">s are</span> stored so next time when you run KUBE <span lang="EN-US">the selected option</span> will be used. These options are also accessible from <u><span class="Path"><a href="../References/Display_Settings_-_On_Rotate_Pan.htm">System &gt; Preferences - Display - Rotate/Pan/Zoom</a></span></u> dialog.</p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="809" class="whs37">
<col class="whs21">
<col class="whs22">
<col class="whs23">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="17.12%" class="whs24">
<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="73.505%" class="whs25">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="9.375%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Display Custom</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays custom number of points. This depends on the value in <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sample every</b></span> field from <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">System &gt; Display</span></i> dialog. The higher the number is the less number of points will be displayed during rotate or pan.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Display_Custom.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Display Less</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays every 20-th point.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Display_Less.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Display Normal</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays every 10-th point.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Display_Normal.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Display More</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays every point.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Display_More.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="bullet">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head-steptitle">Commands related to the appearance of objects</p>
<p>They are also accessible from <u><span class="Path"><a href="../References/Display_Settings_-_On_Rotate_Pan.htm">System &gt; Preferences - Display - Rotate/Pan/Zoom</a></span></u> dialog. Th<span lang="EN-US">e</span>s<span lang="EN-US">e</span> mode<span lang="EN-US">s are</span> not stored so next time when you run KUBE <span lang="EN-US">the default option -</span> <span class="Mode">Draw Points</span> <span lang="EN-US">-</span> will be used.</p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="811" class="whs38">
<col class="whs21">
<col class="whs22">
<col class="whs23">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="17.12%" class="whs24">
<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="73.505%" class="whs25">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="9.375%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Draw Points</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays objects as points.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Draw_Points.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Draw Shaded Points</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays objects as large shaded points. Note that these points are larger than the points in <span class="Mode">Large Points</span> Render mode. If the vertices are too close to each other in the current view, this mode looks similar to <span class="Mode">Draw Scene</span> mode.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Draw_Shaded_Points.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.12%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Draw Scene</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.505%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Displays objects as their current rendering mode.</p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: Render mode commands and On rotate/pan commands are not applicable for datum entities, probe points, and static stripes.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/On_Rotate_Pan_Draw_Scene.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Static_View_Commands"></a>Static View Commands</p>
<p>They are used for custom visualisation (and quick rendering) of scan and mesh objects in the static scene.</p>
<p><img src="../view_menu/commands_files/Image7.gif" width="256px" height="90px" border="0" class="img_whs39" alt=""></p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="811" class="whs40">
